  "body": "**Fixes #724.** The `camcraft-mcp` skill told agents argument names the server refuses, for 8 tools. This corrects them, brings the gap list current, and adds a test so the skill can't drift from `tools/list` silently again.\n\n**Process change:** `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md` is a process file, so `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` goes 4 -> 5. A suggested #681 line for the merging session:\n\n> **PROCESS_VERSION 5** · PR #(this) · the `camcraft-mcp` skill's tool signatures now match the server (`post` takes `output`, `add_operation` takes `source`, `set_stock` takes `box {dx, dy, dz}` / `cylinder` / `from_model`, `set_operation_area` / `set_operation_geometry` take `operation`, `set_work_offset` takes `word`, `load_machine` takes `builtin` / `path` / `clear`, `add_tool` takes `catalog`), and its gap list is current. **Fork action:** pull the process files; an agent that learned the old names should use the new ones.\n\n### What changed\n\n- **`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`, the tool reference:** the 8 drifted entries now use the names the server publishes. The list is in #724.\n- **`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`, \"Known Remaining Gaps\":**\n  - Moved to \"shipped\": pocket recognition (#35, `detect_pockets`), in-plane part axes (#557, `set_part_axes`), and the live GUI session (#183, #567, `--mcp-port` / `mcp --connect`). Also three-point alignment (#555, `lay_part_on_points`) and the fixture locate (#561, `locate_part`), which merged while this PR was open (3961e031).\n  - `MoveModel` and `RepairModel` now point to their open PRs, #719 and #721.\n  - Face-to-plane alignment (#330) is noted as GUI-only.\n- **`crates/app/tests/mcp_skill_signatures.rs` (new), the drift alarm:** for every `` - `name { … }` `` signature in the skill, the tool must exist, each top-level documented key must be an `inputSchema` property, and each required argument must be documented.\n  - A floor on how many signatures it finds (30; the skill has 34) keeps a format change from making it pass on nothing.\n  - `the_key_reader_takes_top_level_keys_only` pins the small parser itself: quoted values and nested object fields aren't arguments.\n- **`.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`:** 4 -> 5.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/724-mcp-skill-signatures.md`.\n\nNo product code changes.\n\n### What ran (Windows 10, local)\n\nFork: `austin62jake/Camcraft2`, `main` at upstream f42d3788 (contains v0.16.0, PROCESS_VERSION 4). Gated on 47a7d0e7.\n\n- **Quick gate plan:** `mcp_skill_signatures`, 2 passed.\n- **The same test on `main`'s skill** (the file put back for the run): it fails with 13 named lines across 6 tools. For example: `line 106: post has no argument \"path\" (it takes {\"output\", \"post\"})`, `line 93: add_operation has no argument \"model\"`, `line 99: set_operation_area requires \"area\", which the skill leaves out`. The other 2 of the 8 (`set_stock`, `add_tool`) were wrong in their prose, which the test doesn't read.\n- **Clippy:** `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`, clean.\n- **Not run:** Linux, macOS, other suites (no product code changed).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #724\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
